====Climate in Yagikoshu====
Yagikoshu, the southernmost island, spans from 20°S to 26.9°S. The climate is predominantly [[w:Humid subtropical climate|humid subtropical]] (''Cfa'') with warm temperate characteristics at higher elevations and in the far south.<ref name="oma2024">{{cite report |author=Okaiken Meteorological Agency |date=2024 |title=Climate Atlas of Okaiken: 1991–2020 Normals |series=OMA Technical Report No. 114 |location=Okami |publisher=Government Press}}</ref> This region represents the most temperate part of Okaiken, though it is not sub-arctic as previously described in historical documents. Summers are hot and humid, with temperatures ranging from 28°C to 35°C, while winters are mild, typically ranging from 10°C to 20°C. Frost occurs only at higher elevations or during exceptional cold snaps, and snow is virtually unknown at sea level. The traditional observance of the "Day of the Frost" on June 21 marks the coolest period of the year but does not indicate regular snowfall.

